            "review_text": "Bryon K\nOsoyoos, Canada99 contributions\n0\nVery bright and clean place\nJan 2020\nI visited the second location, 120 Nguyen Thai Binh. I went because a local food blog had suggested it might be in the top 5 place for Pho. With these expectations I was a little disappointed. First surprise was that they don’t use pho noodle, but use bun. No effect on the taste but very non traditional in my understanding. And to my experience the noodles were over cooked. Supposedly top pho broth is very clear, this one a bit cloudy. \nOverall it was no better, perhaps not as good as the place local to my apartment who only charges about half as much. I think Phu Vuong suffers some from operating like a production line. If you are close to a more traditional place I wouldn’t suggest making a journey.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 1, 2020",
